DIAGNOSE, NICHT FUER DIE SERIE -- pinctrl: sunxi: mask a PIO parent
interrupt that asserts with an empty status register

This is a measuring instrument, not a fix. Apply it only if the device
still hangs with 0143, and take it out again afterwards.

What it buys: today a PIO bank interrupt that fires while the bank's own
status register reads zero is an unrecoverable live-lock. The GIC is a
fasteoi chip, so chained_irq_enter() masks nothing and chained_irq_exit()
only EOIs; if the demux finds no status bit to clear, the line stays high
and the CPU re-enters the same handler forever. Nothing is logged, no
counter in /proc/interrupts moves, and the console goes quiet -- which is
exactly the picture in analyse/boot/board-mgr-hang-20260911.txt.

With this hunk the same event masks the offending parent once and prints

    sunxi-pio: parent irq N (bank index B, hw bank H, status reg 0xR)
    asserted with an empty status register -- masking it

so the device stays alive and the console names the GIC line that
actually carries the PH bank's EINT. That number is the one open question
behind 0143: 0143 asserts PH = GIC SPI 60 on the strength of the vendor
driver's own index-based lookup, not on a register read of this SoC.

Price: the bank whose parent gets masked loses its interrupts for the
rest of the boot, and a genuinely spurious single assert would cost a
bank the same way. That is acceptable for one measurement run and not
acceptable in the series -- which is why this is a separate file.

Applies with or without 0143 (it touches a different part of the file).

--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c
@@ -1266,6 +1266,21 @@
 		for_each_set_bit(irqoffset, &val, IRQ_PER_BANK)
 			generic_handle_domain_irq(pctl->domain,
 						  bank * IRQ_PER_BANK + irqoffset);
+	} else {
+		/*
+		 * DIAGNOSIS ONLY -- do not merge into the series.
+		 *
+		 * The parent line asserted, but this bank's status register is
+		 * empty, so nothing here can clear the source. The GIC is a
+		 * fasteoi chip, so chained_irq_enter() does not mask and
+		 * chained_irq_exit() only EOIs: the line stays high and the
+		 * CPU takes the same interrupt again immediately, forever.
+		 * Mask it at the parent instead and name the line -- that
+		 * number is the measurement we are after.
+		 */
+		pr_err("sunxi-pio: parent irq %u (bank index %lu, hw bank %u, status reg 0x%lx) asserted with an empty status register -- masking it\n",
+		       irq, bank, sunxi_irq_hw_bank_num(pctl->desc, bank), reg);
+		chip->irq_mask(&desc->irq_data);
 	}
 
 	chained_irq_exit(chip, desc);
